#!/usr/bin/env bash
# 검수 2차: Antigravity 의 시각과 애니메이션 감사(원본 빌드 대 결과 빌드). 저장소 루트에서 실행.
cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." || exit 1
PROMPT='First read migration-audit/BRIEF.md, migration-audit/MIGRATION_SPEC.md, migration-audit/MISSION.md sections 5, 7 and 11, and migration-audit/motion/ANIMATION_INVENTORY.md (sections on reachable animations and the opening timeline). You are the visual, interaction and animation lead. This is QA cycle 2 of 3: the visual and animation audit of the RESULT build against the ORIGINAL build. Run every command in the foreground and wait for it; do not start background tasks; write your report file before you end even if some steps could not be completed. Rules: do not modify any file under web/ or any existing document; no git commands that change anything; no next build. You may create files only under migration-audit/harness/agy2/, migration-audit/screenshots/cycle2-agy/ and migration-audit/motion/cycle2-agy/, plus the one report migration-audit/CYCLE2_agy.md. The two builds are served locally and are static exports of the same app: ORIGINAL (baseline commit 63445c7, identical to the deployed site) at http://127.0.0.1:4175/voila-test-aresjoo/ and RESULT (branch migration-result) at http://127.0.0.1:4176/voila-test-aresjoo/ (if 4176 answers 404 for /ko/ wait one minute and retry; its files were still being copied). Playwright is in web/node_modules; reuse web/scripts/capture/states.mjs (makeState, installState) to seed logged-in states and look at migration-audit/harness/lib/common.mjs for the determinism controls already worked out (fixed clock, fonts ready, images decoded, disable checker imaging, reduced motion for still shots). Everything is a browser-only test ledger with fake money; you may open boxes and take items in seeded states, but do not submit a withdrawal or a shipping request. INTENDED differences between the builds (everything else must be identical): (1) sample reviews: the review section on box detail pages, the /reviews screen, the rating line and review count on box cards on the home grid, the review detail sheet, the first header link on a box page (its text holds the review count); (2) wallet history lists opening and take transactions, negative amounts read -$1 instead of $-1; (3) the account password sheet can complete (success state, one new line for accounts without an authenticator app); (4) the confirm dialog ignores presses for 350 ms after it appears, with no visual change; (5) nothing else, in particular the home hero banner, the opening animation, the multi-result screen, the purchase bar, the contents grid, odds tables, inventory, verify, wins, guide, legal, account screens and all sheets other than the review detail sheet must look and move exactly as in ORIGINAL. Do: (A) animation: record the opening of one box and of five boxes on both builds with the same seeded state and fixed seeds, frames every 50 ms from the press to the settled result, normal and reduced motion, at 390 and 1440 width; compare phase by phase (start frame, mid frames, peak, end frame), measured durations, order of class or attribute changes on the opening root, and the final result screen; also record the home hero banner cycle on both builds (several seconds of frames) and compare. Report every difference with the frame files. (B) stills outside the intended areas: for each of these on both builds at 390 and 1440 in ko, en and zh compare element by element (bounding boxes within 2px, text, line counts, computed font and color of the primitives): header, footer, home hero, search and category chips, a box card without its rating line, box page hero and purchase bar, contents tiles, odds summary and tables, notes, inventory (seeded), wallet (seeded), withdraw form, verify, wins, guide, legal, account, and every sheet you can open (menu, login, signup, charge, balance, take and its confirm, item detail, verify sheet, language and currency controls, review write form). (C) the intended areas: judge them as a designer against DESIGN.md (one white pill primary button per screen, at most two underlined links, no extra colors, badges or shadows) and against the rest of the app: review rows, product card, photo, rating block, the more button, /reviews at 320, 390, 768, 1440 in three languages, wallet history rows with the new transactions and the minus sign, the password sheet states. Report text overflow, truncation, wrapping, overlap, inconsistent spacing or type size, anything that looks machine-made or broken. (D) hover and focus-visible states of buttons, links, chips, cards and the new review row on both builds at 1280. Grade each finding P0 to P3 using the mission definitions and say whether it is a difference from ORIGINAL (unintended), a quality problem inside an intended area, or a property of ORIGINAL that is unchanged. Never claim to have seen or run something you did not. Separate: seen on screen, read in code, ran myself (with the command), guess. Write in Korean, no em dash characters, no middle dot characters, no exclamation marks. Link every finding to a screenshot or frame file. End with one line stating how many unintended differences you found and a list of what you could not run.'
rtk agy --dangerously-skip-permissions --model gemini-3.8-flash-high --effort high --print "$PROMPT" > migration-audit/logs/agy-cycle2-run.log 2>&1
echo "done cycle2 exit $?"
ls -la migration-audit/CYCLE2_agy.md 2>&1 | cut -c1-120
